# No trailing slash, and it matters. The browser suites are ESM, so `import
# { chromium } from 'playwright'` will not read NODE_PATH, and the way they find the
# sandbox's global packages is a node_modules SYMLINK at the repo root. Git treats a
# symlink as a file, so `node_modules/` does not match it and it turns up untracked on
# every test run. This form covers the directory and the link alike.
node_modules
football/build/.cache/
cfb/build/.cache/

# Fonts cached by scripts/setlist/make_brand.mjs
.cache/

# Local data exports (scripts/pull-ps-runs.mjs)
ps_runs_export.csv

# Browser-test copies of the games, rebuilt from source before every test run.
# These MUST NOT be committed: the site deploys straight from main, so a tracked
# football/__test.html would publish a copy of the game at runthe.gg with the real
# auth client swapped out for a stub. They are build output, not source -- delete
# them freely, the harness writes them again.
# The prefix, not one name: the next throwaway will not be called __test either. One
# called __smoke has already been written here, and it was only kept out of a commit by
# being listed by hand.
__*.html
__authstub.js
